NetApp StorageGrid at a Glance
StorageGrid is NetApp's enterprise object storage solution. Think of it as a distributed system for storing massive amounts of unstructured data (documents, images, videos, backups) with built-in security, high availability, and policy-driven management.

Why it matters:

S3-compatible (works with standard AWS S3 tools)
Deployed across multiple sites for disaster recovery
Handles petabyte-scale data
Automated data lifecycle policies
Used for archival, backup, media, cloud-native apps, and compliance storage

Core Components You'll See
Storage Nodes - The workhorses that actually store your data
Admin Nodes - The control center (web UI, monitoring, configuration)
Gateway Nodes - The front door (load-balance client requests, S3/Swift protocol)
Archive Nodes (optional) - Connect to external storage (tape, cloud)
Grid Network - Connects everything together

Key Concepts to Master
ILM (Information Lifecycle Management) - Policies that automatically move/protect/delete data based on age, size, type, etc.
Erasure Coding - Protec ts data across multiple nodes (like RAID but distributed)
Replication - Creates copies of data across sites
Multi-tenancy - Multiple customers can have isolated storage buckets
Grid Manager UI - Your main management dashboard

