Core Troubleshooting Areas for TSE Role
1. Configuration Issues (Most Common)
Node Communication Problems

Symptoms: Nodes won't join grid, network errors, connectivity alarms
Causes: VLAN misconfiguration, firewalls blocking ports, wrong IPs/DNS, MTU issues
Diagnosis: Grid Manager → Nodes → check network status, verify DNS, test inter-node connectivity
Pro tip: Validate all network requirements (IPs, subnets, gateways, firewalls) BEFORE anything else
S3/Swift Endpoint Issues

Symptoms: Clients can't connect, auth failures, 403 Forbidden, 503 Service Unavailable
Causes: Wrong endpoint config, SSL cert issues, invalid credentials, firewall blocking
Diagnosis: Review endpoint config in Grid Manager, check cert validity, validate access/secret keys
Logs to check: /var/local/log/bycast.log, /var/local/log/servermanager.log
Storage Pool & ILM Misconfiguration

Symptoms: Objects not placed correctly, ILM failure alarms
Causes: Bad storage pool definitions, unrealistic replication requirements, wrong rule order
Diagnosis: Use ILM Rule Simulation tool in Grid Manager to test placement
Fix: Ensure rules match actual topology (e.g., don't require 3 replicas across 2 sites)
2. Performance Bottlenecks
High Latency / Slow Throughput

Root causes:
CPU/disk/network resource exhaustion
Overloaded nodes or sites
Suboptimal ILM causing excessive data movement
Diagnostics:
Grid Manager → Nodes → check CPU, memory, disk I/O usage
Support → Tools → Metrics → look for spike patterns
Review ILM rules for unnecessary ingest/migration workflows
Metadata Service Bottlenecks

Symptoms: Slow object listings/searches, grid-wide degradation
Cause: Under-provisioned metadata services, too many concurrent requests
Fix: Scale out admin/metadata nodes per NetApp recommendations
Full/Near-Full Storage

Symptoms: Low disk space alarms, write throttling, object failures
Fix: Add storage nodes/disks, proactively monitor capacity via dashboards
Network Issues

Symptoms: Packet loss, dropped connections between nodes/clients
Check: MTU settings (standardize for jumbo frames), VLAN configs, routing, network interface errors
3. Backup & Replication Failures
ILM Placement Failures

"Cannot satisfy placement rule" errors → Not enough nodes/sites/capacity
"Replication failed" → Network partition, insufficient available nodes, disk full
Steps:
Check Alarms & Events in Grid Manager
Verify all nodes/sites in ILM rules are online & healthy
Audit logs for ILMP/ILMF error codes
Confirm storage pools have capacity
Check inter-site network connectivity
Data Migration Issues

Symptoms: Node decommissioning stuck, data not migrated
Cause: Active connections, unmet prerequisites
Fix: Follow decommissioning checklist, resolve blocking alarms, let background jobs complete
