Best Practices
Match host NQN exactly
Validate zoning and routing before deep troubleshooting
Keep firmware and drivers aligned
Use consistent MTU on NVMe/TCP paths
Confirm namespace mapping
Check both host and array logs
Validate switch/fabric health for FC
Final Support Tip
When troubleshooting NVMe over fabrics, always confirm:

fabric/network path works
host NQN is authorized
namespace exists and is mapped
target port is reachable
correct driver/firmware versions are in use
